WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.327
(package clunks)

00:00:01.327 --> 00:00:03.252
(upbeat music)

00:00:03.252 --> 00:00:06.169
(plastic rustling)

00:00:09.690 --> 00:00:12.806
- So yeah, this smartwatch is $69.

00:00:12.806 --> 00:00:16.890
But, but, before you
type it, is it though?

00:00:16.890 --> 00:00:18.060
Is it really that nice?

00:00:18.060 --> 00:00:19.200
Is it that good?

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:20.640
I feel like we should define good first,

00:00:20.640 --> 00:00:21.997
because going into this, I was thinking,

00:00:21.997 --> 00:00:23.077
"Just the fact that you can get

00:00:23.077 --> 00:00:26.070
"a fully functioning
smartwatch for $69 in 2023,"

00:00:26.070 --> 00:00:29.010
just that by itself, on its
face, was kind of amazing.

00:00:29.010 --> 00:00:29.843
'Cause we live in a world

00:00:29.843 --> 00:00:31.230
where you can easily spend hundreds

00:00:31.230 --> 00:00:32.940
and hundreds of dollars on a smartwatch.

00:00:32.940 --> 00:00:34.500
But clearly, there's a wide spectrum

00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:36.210
of what these things can be capable of.

00:00:36.210 --> 00:00:39.600
So this one, just the simple stuff, right?

00:00:39.600 --> 00:00:43.560
Just the basics, the time,
notifications, step counter,

00:00:43.560 --> 00:00:46.140
heart rate, calorie
counter, sleep tracking,

00:00:46.140 --> 00:00:48.390
just on its face, that's good enough

00:00:48.390 --> 00:00:51.120
for 95% of people, right?

00:00:51.120 --> 00:00:52.620
Well, let's just start
with the basics here.

00:00:52.620 --> 00:00:54.990
This is a square smartwatch.

00:00:54.990 --> 00:00:57.327
It's got this orange silicon
band that comes in the box

00:00:57.327 --> 00:00:59.190
and it feels surprisingly similar

00:00:59.190 --> 00:01:00.450
to any other smartwatch band.

00:01:00.450 --> 00:01:03.450
And then it's got a
1.96-inch diagonal display.

00:01:03.450 --> 00:01:05.940
The color is metallic gray,

00:01:05.940 --> 00:01:09.840
but the material here is
definitely not nearly as metallic.

00:01:09.840 --> 00:01:12.030
It does say aluminum alloy on their site,

00:01:12.030 --> 00:01:14.010
but if you didn't tell
me that, just holding it,

00:01:14.010 --> 00:01:16.860
I would swear this is 100%
made of plastic on the outside.

00:01:16.860 --> 00:01:18.150
But, you know, at least it's coated

00:01:18.150 --> 00:01:20.250
in sort of a matte finish on the back part

00:01:20.250 --> 00:01:22.530
that's touching your wrist
around the heart rate sensors.

00:01:22.530 --> 00:01:24.960
And then there's some
engravings with a bunch of text

00:01:24.960 --> 00:01:27.240
in the Nothing font, like the model number

00:01:27.240 --> 00:01:28.500
and the headquarters location,

00:01:28.500 --> 00:01:31.020
which happens to be Cheapside, London,

00:01:31.020 --> 00:01:33.060
which is very appropriate.

00:01:33.060 --> 00:01:35.460
Honestly, it doesn't
look or feel terrible,

00:01:35.460 --> 00:01:38.130
but it just, it clearly has
all the obvious shortcuts

00:01:38.130 --> 00:01:40.770
of a cheap product the more
you look closely at it.

00:01:40.770 --> 00:01:42.210
You know, the bezels are thick

00:01:42.210 --> 00:01:44.850
and also weirdly uneven
all the way around.

00:01:44.850 --> 00:01:47.760
There is no rotating dial,
just the single shallow,

00:01:47.760 --> 00:01:50.580
cheap feeling button right
above the small tinny speaker

00:01:50.580 --> 00:01:54.000
to the side and no fancy
puck to charge, just USBA

00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:56.340
to dual pin cable that comes in the box.

00:01:56.340 --> 00:01:58.200
It magnetizes to the
back, which in hindsight,

00:01:58.200 --> 00:02:00.600
I guess is just as
convenient as a fancy puck,

00:02:00.600 --> 00:02:02.550
but, you know, a little
less elegant looking.

00:02:02.550 --> 00:02:05.910
But I guess, the key here is
all of it works and it's solid.

00:02:05.910 --> 00:02:09.540
Like, the brightness outside,
it gets up to 600 nits.

00:02:09.540 --> 00:02:10.740
There's no auto brightness though,

00:02:10.740 --> 00:02:13.530
so you gotta change brightness
manually, like this.

00:02:13.530 --> 00:02:16.650
But hey, at its max, it's
very good indoors, at least.

00:02:16.650 --> 00:02:19.500
And the whole thing is IP68
water and dust resistant,

00:02:19.500 --> 00:02:22.110
which is, first of all,
great if you want to go out

00:02:22.110 --> 00:02:24.240
and sweat in it or go out in the rain.

00:02:24.240 --> 00:02:26.610
But also wasn't there
a long period of time

00:02:26.610 --> 00:02:29.730
where OnePlus and Nothing
products didn't get IP certified

00:02:29.730 --> 00:02:31.530
'cause it cost too much extra?

00:02:31.530 --> 00:02:33.570
But now, the CMF watch has it,

00:02:33.570 --> 00:02:35.620
but then it all works with the
CMF Watch app on your phone,

00:02:35.620 --> 00:02:38.460
which is where all the data
gets sent via Bluetooth.

00:02:38.460 --> 00:02:41.220
So honestly, there's not too
many different clever ways

00:02:41.220 --> 00:02:43.140
to design a watch UI,

00:02:43.140 --> 00:02:44.820
so, you know, if you get a smart watch,

00:02:44.820 --> 00:02:46.260
if you've used one before,

00:02:46.260 --> 00:02:48.180
you'll basically already
know how to use this one.

00:02:48.180 --> 00:02:49.800
So your watch face is your starting point.

00:02:49.800 --> 00:02:52.290
And then you can swipe
through fitness data,

00:02:52.290 --> 00:02:55.230
which looks surprisingly
like Apple Watch rings.

00:02:55.230 --> 00:02:57.540
It's got your heart rate
history for the past 24 hours.

00:02:57.540 --> 00:03:00.270
The weather is there in
that simple dot matrix way,

00:03:00.270 --> 00:03:02.310
plus sleep time if you
use it to track sleep,

00:03:02.310 --> 00:03:04.890
then a single press on
that plastic feeling button

00:03:04.890 --> 00:03:06.270
will take you to your app list,

00:03:06.270 --> 00:03:08.700
which you can view as a grid or as a list.

00:03:08.700 --> 00:03:09.930
And then there's a good
amount of apps in here

00:03:09.930 --> 00:03:11.400
that just come on the watch.

00:03:11.400 --> 00:03:14.310
So an exercise app that has
a ton of different exercises,

00:03:14.310 --> 00:03:15.690
the blood oxygen app,

00:03:15.690 --> 00:03:17.550
which gives you your
measurements whenever you want.

00:03:17.550 --> 00:03:19.170
You've also got a phone call app

00:03:19.170 --> 00:03:21.510
and yes, you can receive
phone calls on the watch

00:03:21.510 --> 00:03:24.150
and that tinny little
speaker will crank out audio

00:03:24.150 --> 00:03:26.880
as loud as it can to
facilitate a real conversation.

00:03:26.880 --> 00:03:28.260
There's also a music app,

00:03:28.260 --> 00:03:29.640
which gives you just music controls

00:03:29.640 --> 00:03:31.680
for whenever something
is playing on your phone.

00:03:31.680 --> 00:03:33.870
There's even a camera remote app,

00:03:33.870 --> 00:03:37.140
which it doesn't actually open
the camera app on my phone

00:03:37.140 --> 00:03:38.670
or show a viewfinder preview,

00:03:38.670 --> 00:03:40.500
but when I do have the camera app open,

00:03:40.500 --> 00:03:43.110
the shutter button does
actually work, so there's that.

00:03:43.110 --> 00:03:44.820
There's even a voice assistant app,

00:03:44.820 --> 00:03:46.980
which if you open it, basically
just opens Google Assistant

00:03:46.980 --> 00:03:48.270
on your phone and then uses the mics

00:03:48.270 --> 00:03:50.247
and speakers on the watch
for you to interact with it.

00:03:50.247 --> 00:03:52.770
The Find My Phone app is hilarious though.

00:03:52.770 --> 00:03:56.490
It only works when the CMF app is open

00:03:56.490 --> 00:03:57.720
or running on the phone.

00:03:57.720 --> 00:03:59.220
So if you've just closed the app,

00:03:59.220 --> 00:04:01.560
it will just ask you to
open the app on your phone,

00:04:01.560 --> 00:04:03.000
but you don't have your phone.

00:04:03.000 --> 00:04:04.500
But when you do actually open it,

00:04:04.500 --> 00:04:07.623
so it plays this max volume ringing sound,

00:04:08.610 --> 00:04:10.320
which will allow you to find the phone,

00:04:10.320 --> 00:04:13.380
which is pretty cool as long
as you've got that app open

00:04:13.380 --> 00:04:14.760
or have opened it recently.

00:04:14.760 --> 00:04:17.070
And I will say the UI on the watch itself,

00:04:17.070 --> 00:04:19.080
it feels like it's moving
around pretty quickly

00:04:19.080 --> 00:04:21.810
and not too much waiting
time to actually open

00:04:21.810 --> 00:04:23.280
or switch between these apps,

00:04:23.280 --> 00:04:24.780
mostly because they're very lightweight.

00:04:24.780 --> 00:04:27.420
Like, this thing is basically
just a Bluetooth accessory,

00:04:27.420 --> 00:04:29.280
pinging little controls on your phone

00:04:29.280 --> 00:04:30.720
and then it's got watch faces

00:04:30.720 --> 00:04:32.580
and the watch faces have
a nice little variety.

00:04:32.580 --> 00:04:34.110
I think this one's probably my favorite

00:04:34.110 --> 00:04:35.160
with the orange theme

00:04:35.160 --> 00:04:38.520
and a second hand moving slowly
in a full circle down here.

00:04:38.520 --> 00:04:40.080
I feel like I'm pretty impressed.

00:04:40.080 --> 00:04:41.550
It's also very lightweight,

00:04:41.550 --> 00:04:45.600
not that people always value
lightweight in watches,

00:04:45.600 --> 00:04:47.130
but in this price range,

00:04:47.130 --> 00:04:48.600
they're pretty much all
gonna be made of plastic.

00:04:48.600 --> 00:04:49.710
So you might as well lean into it.

00:04:49.710 --> 00:04:52.620
And this thing is super light,
so if you're doing sports

00:04:52.620 --> 00:04:55.710
or just running around, yeah,
it's kind of out of the way.

00:04:55.710 --> 00:04:58.290
And then because it's
a Bluetooth accessory

00:04:58.290 --> 00:05:00.780
and a pretty generic one,
you can use this actually

00:05:00.780 --> 00:05:02.310
with basically any Android phone.

00:05:02.310 --> 00:05:06.600
So you just grab the Play
Store app, which has 3.1 stars

00:05:06.600 --> 00:05:09.240
and it does have some connection
issues occasionally for me.

00:05:09.240 --> 00:05:11.280
But even that sort of
availability, at least,

00:05:11.280 --> 00:05:13.830
on any Android phone is
better than Apple can say

00:05:13.830 --> 00:05:14.820
about their own smartwatch.

00:05:14.820 --> 00:05:17.040
And it gives me all the
basic info I'm looking for

00:05:17.040 --> 00:05:20.550
from heart rate history
to workout summaries.

00:05:20.550 --> 00:05:22.500
Honestly, it's not so
bad when it's working.

00:05:22.500 --> 00:05:24.720
So I'm also able to do sleep tracking,

00:05:24.720 --> 00:05:27.120
since that only really requires
the heart rate sensors.

00:05:27.120 --> 00:05:29.940
But I also continue to get
that info from the sensors

00:05:29.940 --> 00:05:31.950
that are actually built into
the mattress cover I use.

00:05:31.950 --> 00:05:33.780
At this point, I'm sure
you've heard of Eight Sleep

00:05:33.780 --> 00:05:36.120
and the Pod Mattress Cover
that, you know, warms up

00:05:36.120 --> 00:05:38.490
and cools down each side
of the bed independently,

00:05:38.490 --> 00:05:39.330
automatically.

00:05:39.330 --> 00:05:41.490
So that thing not only
helps you sleep better

00:05:41.490 --> 00:05:42.900
by automatically changing
the temperatures,

00:05:42.900 --> 00:05:44.580
but then it also monitors how you sleep.

00:05:44.580 --> 00:05:45.690
It's got the sensors inside

00:05:45.690 --> 00:05:47.040
and then delivers a report for you.

00:05:47.040 --> 00:05:48.360
So you just open the app every morning,

00:05:48.360 --> 00:05:49.620
you get this personalized report

00:05:49.620 --> 00:05:51.900
that shows you things like
your heart rate variance,

00:05:51.900 --> 00:05:53.160
respiratory rate, you know,

00:05:53.160 --> 00:05:55.140
how your sleep stages
panned out overnight.

00:05:55.140 --> 00:05:58.260
So I think I'm officially
done wearing any wearables

00:05:58.260 --> 00:06:00.570
to sleep for any sleep tracking data,

00:06:00.570 --> 00:06:01.740
just 'cause this handles it all.

00:06:01.740 --> 00:06:02.940
Now, I've actually
talked about them before

00:06:02.940 --> 00:06:04.920
and I saw a lot of your
comments about Eight Sleep.

00:06:04.920 --> 00:06:07.470
And so I chatted with
Eight Sleep about them

00:06:07.470 --> 00:06:08.820
and was able to get them to offer

00:06:08.820 --> 00:06:11.310
a little bit more functionality
to people who are new,

00:06:11.310 --> 00:06:12.930
like, first time signing up.

00:06:12.930 --> 00:06:14.280
So they'll actually now,

00:06:14.280 --> 00:06:16.050
no matter what your membership level,

00:06:16.050 --> 00:06:19.650
they will give you a free
Sleep Report every six months,

00:06:19.650 --> 00:06:21.300
so it's not behind any sort of paywall.

00:06:21.300 --> 00:06:23.070
So thanks to Eight Sleep
for sponsoring this video.

00:06:23.070 --> 00:06:24.930
I'm happy to report that
they're also offering

00:06:24.930 --> 00:06:27.870
you guys the largest
discount that they ever have.

00:06:27.870 --> 00:06:28.860
So if you wanna check it out,

00:06:28.860 --> 00:06:30.780
feel free to check out the
link in the description

00:06:30.780 --> 00:06:32.340
and use code MKBHD.

00:06:32.340 --> 00:06:34.320
So now that I'm not wearing it to sleep,

00:06:34.320 --> 00:06:37.050
I am able to charge the
CMF Watch every night.

00:06:37.050 --> 00:06:39.630
Like I said, it's got this
little magnetic pin charger,

00:06:39.630 --> 00:06:41.190
technically not as pretty

00:06:41.190 --> 00:06:43.200
as those fancy wireless charging pucks,

00:06:43.200 --> 00:06:44.610
but honestly, pretty close.

00:06:44.610 --> 00:06:48.600
And the battery life, I've
realized, is really, really good

00:06:48.600 --> 00:06:49.800
because of how simple it is.

00:06:49.800 --> 00:06:52.140
Again, just a Bluetooth accessory,

00:06:52.140 --> 00:06:54.300
not a whole ton of
processing power needed.

00:06:54.300 --> 00:06:56.100
On their site, they're claiming, like,

00:06:56.100 --> 00:06:57.750
13 days of regular use.

00:06:57.750 --> 00:06:59.280
I don't know if I'm gonna get that,

00:06:59.280 --> 00:07:02.580
but I was able to get three
straight days easy, no problem.

00:07:02.580 --> 00:07:04.980
And I'm sure you could
probably use Power Saver mode

00:07:04.980 --> 00:07:06.450
and get even more if you wanted to.

00:07:06.450 --> 00:07:09.750
So it's got better battery
life than an Apple Watch.

00:07:09.750 --> 00:07:11.190
But really, the main thing that I learned,

00:07:11.190 --> 00:07:13.530
when testing this watch, is it turns out,

00:07:13.530 --> 00:07:18.427
this is actually a pretty
expensive watch in its segment.

00:07:18.427 --> 00:07:23.427
$69 is on the premium end
for a very basic smartwatch.

00:07:24.543 --> 00:07:26.670
It's actually pretty
common for the cheapest,

00:07:26.670 --> 00:07:30.930
most basic smartwatches to
be in the 20 to $50 range.

00:07:30.930 --> 00:07:31.800
And, you know, at that point,

00:07:31.800 --> 00:07:33.960
they're all, more or
less, the same product.

00:07:33.960 --> 00:07:36.870
They're all a simple,
plastic-y Bluetooth accessory

00:07:36.870 --> 00:07:38.700
with some slightly different designs.

00:07:38.700 --> 00:07:43.700
So this, the CMF Watch Pro is
a slightly better packaged,

00:07:44.490 --> 00:07:47.190
slightly better design,
slightly better looking version

00:07:47.190 --> 00:07:50.550
for a slightly upcharge,
kind of the same way Nothing

00:07:50.550 --> 00:07:52.260
is probably charging a little bit more

00:07:52.260 --> 00:07:54.750
than you would expect for a
phone with the same specs,

00:07:54.750 --> 00:07:55.620
just 'cause of the design

00:07:55.620 --> 00:07:56.610
and the nice stuff they do with it.

00:07:56.610 --> 00:07:58.350
That's what this is too.

00:07:58.350 --> 00:07:59.880
And I bring up Nothing because CMF

00:07:59.880 --> 00:08:02.940
is Nothing's ultra-budget sub-brand

00:08:02.940 --> 00:08:05.490
and they actually do some
other stuff, like earphones,

00:08:05.490 --> 00:08:08.460
chargers, same deal,
extremely cheap products,

00:08:08.460 --> 00:08:10.110
but just marked up a little bit

00:08:10.110 --> 00:08:11.970
for nice packaging and nice design.

00:08:11.970 --> 00:08:13.830
So here, I'll leave you with this.

00:08:13.830 --> 00:08:17.730
CMF, in the industries,
typically stands for color,

00:08:17.730 --> 00:08:18.960
material, finish.

00:08:18.960 --> 00:08:19.793
It's the name of the company,

00:08:19.793 --> 00:08:22.590
but it's also what
those letters stand for.

00:08:22.590 --> 00:08:26.040
And the CMF of this smartwatch

00:08:26.040 --> 00:08:30.660
is it's very much still
silver-ish, fingerprint-y,

00:08:30.660 --> 00:08:33.540
technically metal, but
feels kind of plastic-y.

00:08:33.540 --> 00:08:35.730
But if you squint enough,

00:08:35.730 --> 00:08:39.780
this square kind of looks
like an Apple Watch Ultra.

00:08:39.780 --> 00:08:41.850
And if that's your comparison point,

00:08:41.850 --> 00:08:44.460
then this thing is a total bargain.

00:08:44.460 --> 00:08:47.340
So I think that was what
their real goal was.

00:08:47.340 --> 00:08:49.440
Yeah, if you wanna get one
of these things, you can.

00:08:49.440 --> 00:08:52.320
It is maybe a little more
challenging to get it in the U.S.

00:08:52.320 --> 00:08:54.810
Maybe if you import it,
spend a couple extra dollars,

00:08:54.810 --> 00:08:56.970
then you're competing with
some other smartwatches,

00:08:56.970 --> 00:08:58.053
but it's an option.

00:08:58.890 --> 00:09:00.840
But now you know it exists.

00:09:00.840 --> 00:09:02.280
The more you know.

00:09:02.280 --> 00:09:05.213
Thanks for watching, catch you
guys in the next one, peace.

00:09:06.101 --> 00:09:09.101
(soft upbeat music)

